# Auto commit & push

After finishing a task that changes project files, **commit and push to `origin` without waiting for the user to ask.**

## When

- Do this at the end of a completed change set (feature, fix, content update, etc.)
- Skip empty commits (no file changes)
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, API keys)

## How

Follow the repo’s normal commit protocol (status, diff, log style, HEREDOC message), then:

1. Stage relevant files
2. Commit with a concise message focused on why
3. `git push` to the tracked remote branch (usually `origin/main`)
4. Confirm success with a brief status note to the user

## Still require explicit ask for

- Force push, hard reset, rebase onto remote, or other destructive git ops
- Amending commits already pushed (unless the user asks)
